From 5b16ed7e47d1a65bc5947b827c396186e50f71ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:51:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(drill): name each hole wider than the drill, without
 holding the post

detect_holes on a Drill op took holes wider than the drill, and
generate, verify and post passed with no word. Each such hole came out
undersize.

- app: operation::drill_size names each Z hole wider than the
  Drill-kind tool by more than 0.1 mm, in a cycle that drills to size
  (Auto, Drill, Peck, Ream). Detect holes keeps the hole (a pilot is
  valid) and names it in DetectedHoles::undersize; MCP detect_holes
  answers `undersize`, the GUI status line says the same.
- sim: a new advisory Warning::DrillUndersize, one per such hole at its
  first cutting move. It does not hold the post. MCP finding kind
  `drill_undersize`.
- A hole narrower than the drill stays the gouge law's, and the post
  stays held.

Pinned by tests/drill_undersize.rs (the issue's MCP sequence),
operation::drill_size::tests and
detect_holes_on_a_drill_op_keeps_a_wider_hole_and_names_it_undersize.

Fixes #2496

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
